  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_hulstaerti_en/",
      "html": "<p>The Butterfly Barb Barbus hulstaerti reaches 4 cm in length and fascinates by its wonderful colors. It had been lost to the hobby for more than 30 years.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_hulstaerti_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: Congo basin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_hulstaerti_en/",
      "html": "<p>In their area of origin they live in flat, shady and relatively cool jungle waters. The discovery site data indicate water values of pH around 6 and a total hardness under 5 dGH, so no excessive problems for their maintenance are expected.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_hulstaerti_en/",
      "html": "<p>The more delicate males can be differentiated from the larger, chubbier females by the narrower anterior side spot.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_hulstaerti_en/",
      "html": "<p>In August 2006 a somewhat larger number of this fish could be imported for the first time. Due to the complicated political situation in the Congo the availability of wild-caught fish is not secured, therefore ambitious breeders should take care of this swimming gem to secure its existence in our aquaria.</p>"
    }
  ],
